 "format": "citerift-stage04-freeze/3",
 "label": "Stage 04 freeze-3 candidate manifest (final corrective cycle, D-083). Frozen scientific code: the freeze-content commit that holds this file; named with its tree and CI run by the attestation commit that follows it. Not a freeze until the owner accepts it.",
 "limitations": [
  "dt-3 / bib-1 (D-083): a material bibliographic conflict between the citation's own description and any event of the deciding lookup makes the candidate UNRESOLVED_IDENTITY (D-13a), never positive. bib-1 can block a positive, never create, restore or move one (dt-3 equals dt-2 case for case without a conflict: oracle-dt3).",
  "bib-1 recall costs on genuine citations (fail closed; BIBLIOGRAPHIC_SPEC.md section 9): a record that lists fewer authors than the citation, a misspelled or mixed-script record name, a genre word the citation adds to the record title ('Letter: X'), a title in another language, a conflicting bridged or co-keyed event of the same key. On the 243 design-exposed development pairs, 6 pairs (5 citations) abstain that an engineering reading of citation and record (not a label) takes for the retracted work itself (in-sample, never an estimate).",
  "bib-1 residual false compatibility (reviewer finding A-02): a commenter sharing a surname with the work's authors (3.3 % of random record pairs for one cited name), writing a note whose title holds the record's title and no lexicon word, stays positive; so does a related note cited with no comparable author whose extra title words are outside the lexicon or whose designation word is split by an invisible format character (review G-04); free-text references and identifier-only units have no description.",
  "bib-1 size bounds (spec 2.1 steps 1 and 6; reviewer findings E-02 and F-02): a citation source above 16,384 code points, a family above 64 values or a description above 4,096 code points has no description and decides as under dt-2 (development maxima: 5,722 code points, 56 values, 1,804 code points); a crafted unit under the source bound was measured at 6.5 s of parser time (one crafted shape, not a bound).",
  "D-071 recall cost: a citation whose only identifier is given by the checked sources as both the original and a notice (13,681 DOIs and 1,053 PMIDs in one record, 56 DOIs and 27 PMIDs across records, in the pinned snapshot) is UNRESOLVED_IDENTITY (IDENTIFIER_ROLE_COLLISION), never positive, even when the work is truly retracted.",
  "D-072 strict rule kept (D-083 item 5, ROLE_COLLISION_STUDY.md): bib-1 never resolves a role collision. In a same-record collision every event of the lookup describes a retracted work, never the notice, so bib-1 compares the citation with the same fields for both roles and cannot tell them apart; 1,472 of 31,506 dt-1 positive DOI+PMID pairs stay UNRESOLVED_IDENTITY.",
  "D-073 (C-01): a second record of the same work makes a clean retraction abstain (53 snapshot pairs); no same-work-sibling exemption.",
  "D-075: an original DOI cited with the same record's notice PMID stays positive when the DOI is clean; the notice PMID is never positive support.",
  "The 232 development revisions, the 80 first-campaign and the 100 P2 articles are development evidence; the regression on them is not an evaluation, is never rescored and is never counted as unseen data.",
  "D-061 performance: the warm p95 of a retained investigation is above the 5 s target (NOT_MET, D-066); D-064 (per-process verify_index_identity) is not weakened.",
  "Storage: the maximal journal at the Stage 03 caps is 434,316,192 B (1.2x headroom) at 25,753 events per deciding lookup; above 32,030 events per deciding lookup a run is refused (JOURNAL_TOO_LARGE); LOOKUP observation v3 has a measured rho of 13.07 and no analytic bound; the Step 8 candidate-inputs terms have no derived bound (E-09).",
  "C-07: the role-collision scan is quadratic in a lookup's events (2.6 s at 3,000 synthetic events; below 0.03 s on the snapshot's largest keys); measured and retained.",
  "D-062 verification scope (D-064): each process runs verify_index_identity; Stage 02's per-event JSON-Schema pass runs only in Stage 02's complete verify; no tamper case is rejected by that pass alone.",
  "F-11: a descendant that leaves the session by double fork or setsid is attributed and killed only while it is found in the scan; the bound is per attempt, not per investigation.",
  "The external checkpoint (D-052) detects divergence from a recorded state; it is not authentication.",
  "Investigation Memory requires a local POSIX filesystem (rename, fsync, O_NOFOLLOW, flock semantics).",
  "Evaluation labels of a future gate are AI-generated (Stage 03 precedent); not human ground truth.",
  "The Stage 02 snapshot covers Retraction Watch records up to its build; later events are not covered.",
  "The reference models were written by the same engineering process as the production code; their independence is procedural (separate model, oracle and tests), not organisational.",
  "Accepted residuals re-reviewed (D-083 item 7): run idempotency depends on path spelling (use resume --key); a different bundle at the recorded path is STALE; Stage 02 crossref_sources has no ORDER BY (0 rows in the RW-only index)."
 ],
